ansient hog failure did not remain.","evidence_ids":["cmd-664622ee270145c4","cmd-6f3b060231004265","cmd-fe631327fcf9414b","cmd-62839602c6574de6","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct observations cover the healthy baseline, bounded memory-pressure disruption, global OOM selection and termination of the hog, and the API's responsive recovered state without a PID change or restart. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: it includes a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot ID, and recovered service and endpoint state. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["API availability was sampled before, during memory growth, and after the OOM kill rather than continuously at the exact kill instant. The unchanged PID, zero restart count, and successful surrounding responses nevertheless provide strong direct evidence that the service survived.","No persistent application dataset or cluster exists in the captured implementation, so restart recovery evidence appropriately covers service configuration, listener state, and both API endpoints rather than data resynchronization or cluster state."]}
